# ============================================================
#  Appointments (docs/grimoire-script.md §9): when the game deals cards.
#  An appointment deals at an occasion (`at:`), once for each of its subjects (`for:` track kinds you're in, `met`
#  for everyone you've met, nothing for the game itself), the cards it `deals:` (card <id>, pool <id>, trigger <t>, or
#  own: the subject track's cards), while its `when` holds and by its `chance:`. At the month's start a card goes to
#  its `slot:` (else the card's own, else the day's first); at a visit it comes before the drawn cards, or instead of
#  them with `takes: visit`; at a notice it comes next month, in the track's context.
#  The ones below are the game's own, in the order they deal; `use:` names the built-in way each one deals. A new
#  appointment needs no engine code: a market day, a tutoring hour, a named character's café shift.
#  Older spellings still work and mean the same: `trigger: auto` (forced), `ramp:` (milestones), an arc's `beat:`
#  (beats), `replaces: visitN` (festivals), `@place always:` (fixed), `trigger: letter` (letters), `@track intro:` and
#  `start:` (intro, start), `@game exam:` / `appeal:` / `off_shift:` / `spark_cooldown:` (their appointment's card).
# ============================================================

# ---------------- the month's start (after the cards queued for it) ----------------

@appointment forced
desc: Every card with `trigger: auto` whose `when` holds, by its priority.
at: month
deals: trigger auto
use: auto

@appointment beats
desc: The arcs' cards once their arc's clock reaches their `beat:`; at most one plot card a month (two in a month with a beat).
at: month
deals: beats
limit: plot
use: beats

@appointment milestones
desc: Each card with a `ramp:`, for whoever is furthest along: 40% at its low mark, certain at its high mark.
at: month
for: met
deals: ramp
use: ramp

# ---------------- the day's slots ----------------

@appointment class
desc: The course slot: a card from each course you're enrolled in (up to its level) and your thesis; its professor and whoever is there see you.
at: courses
for: course thesis
deals: own
use: courses

@appointment festivals
desc: A card with `replaces: visitN` and a `place:` takes that visit when you go there.
at: visit
deals: replaces
takes: visit
use: festival

@appointment off_shift
desc: Visiting your job's place in term when you aren't working: the hint card comes first.
at: visit
for: job
deals: card job_off_shift
use: off_shift

@appointment fixed
desc: A place's `always:` cards, first on every visit, in order, while their `when` holds.
at: visit
deals: always
use: always

@appointment letters
desc: Away from campus, a letter each night from the letter pool.
at: night
deals: trigger letter
use: letters

# ---------------- notices ----------------

@appointment intro
desc: Joining a track whose lead you haven't met: their `intro:` card, before the track's own.
at: meet lead
deals: intro
use: intro

@appointment start
desc: Enrolling in a course with a `start:` card (the lesson that teaches its spell): it comes the same month.
at: enrol
for: course
deals: start
use: start

@appointment exam
desc: A term's last month: the exam card for each course you're enrolled in.
at: term end
for: course
deals: card course_exam

@appointment appeal
desc: A failed course: the appeal, next month in its context.
at: fail
for: course
deals: card grade_appeal

@appointment warning
desc: A club, job or thesis ending a term below 40 performance.
at: low marks
for: club job thesis
deals: card track_warning

@appointment review
desc: Every job at term end, unless it was the last term: another term, or not.
at: renewal
for: job
deals: card job_term_review

@appointment promotion
desc: A club, job or thesis ending a term at 70 performance with the rank's experience.
at: promotion
for: club job thesis
deals: card track_promotion

@appointment spark_cooldown
desc: Spark with someone crossing the cooldown mark (not with a partner): whether you want this.
at: spark cooldown
for: met
deals: card spark_cooldown
